"""Compare `run` between the oracle (Bazel 9.3.2) and Blaze. See `compare help`."""

import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

USAGE = """\
usage: scripts/run/compare --binary <blaze> [--oracle <bazel>] [--project brotli|re2|all]
                           [--case ID]... [--label NAME] [--skip-oracle]
       scripts/run/compare list
       scripts/run/compare selftest
       scripts/run/compare help

Runs a fixed list of `run` invocations (see `list`) with the oracle and with Blaze, each on its
own work copy of a corpus project (~/.cache/blaze/work/run-compare/<side>/<project>: rsync of
the read-only checkout minus bazel-* and .git, restored to the checkout's git HEAD, plus the
probe package scripts/run/probe as //blaze_run_probe) and its own output user root
(~/.cache/blaze/oracle-out/run-compare-<side>), with a clean environment (HOME, PATH=/usr/bin:/bin
plus the case's variables), --nohome_rc --nosystem_rc, the shared repository cache, --color=no
--curses=no, under systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=12G -p MemorySwapMax=0 with the
supervisor of scripts/lib/compare_common.py, which records how each command really ended (`exit
N`, `signal NAME`, `oom-kill`, `timeout` after 3600 s). Both sides run the same cases in the
same order from a fresh output root. --oracle must be the pinned oracle (sha256 in
UPSTREAM.json); another binary is refused.

Compared per case (after normalising the workspace path, the output user root, the output base
hash, UUIDs and googletest's "(N ms)" timings on each side):
  exit     the termination (exit code, or signal, OOM kill, timeout)
  stdout   the run program's standard output (Bazel writes nothing else to stdout)
  summary  the stderr lines starting with ERROR:, WARNING:, FAIL, "INFO: Running command line",
           "INFO: Runnable command line", "INFO: Build completed", "INFO: Build did NOT", and
           with --subcommands the command description that follows "Running command line:"
  script   (--script_path cases) the written script, then the output of running it

Classes (scripts/lib/compare_common.py): IDENTICAL (every field equal; the oracle exited 0 or
the case declares its exit code in DECLARED_EXIT), DIFFERENT, BOTH-FAILED (equal failures not
declared), NOT-PORTED, ORACLE-UNEXPECTED, SKIPPED.

Output: a header (repository HEAD and dirty flag, both binaries' paths and sha256), a table, the
denominator; raw and normalised outputs under
~/.cache/blaze/run-compare/<label>/<side>/<project>/<case>.{stdout,stderr,norm.json}, and
results.json (with the same provenance and denominator). Exit 0 only when at least one case was
compared and every selected case is IDENTICAL; 1 otherwise (an empty selection included); 2 on
a usage error or a refusal.
--skip-oracle reuses the oracle outputs of an earlier run with the same --label, only when
<label>/oracle/<project>/oracle.key (oracle sha256, this tool's sha256, every case's argv and
environment, the digest of the prepared workspace, the case sequence) equals the key of this
run; otherwise it refuses.
"""

